cs is not interesting at all  has nothing to do with language learning  nothing and there's a lot of  sophisticated  um  i call it pseudo science there  uh  at least that's my reaction to it  and i've expressed myself on this idea  that we have some universal grammar  built into us no i don't believe that i  think the brain just is very good at  developing patterns or seeing patterns  in the in the  range of experience that it's confronted  with because it has to do that in order  that it can then take advantage of the  previous experience to to learn new  things  so um  so you know what's the what's the  concern here uh yes there is this other  word polyglot which means the same thing  most english speakers have never heard  the word polyglot but they have heard  the word linguist  steve is quite the linguist he speaks  more than one language  in the year  2003 i wrote a book  called the linguist a personal guide to  language learning and we started our  first website  for  you know helping people learn english  by and large because of the problem we  saw here with uh immigrants to canada  who couldn't speak english very well and  who weren't very well served by the  classroom model  and we called that site the linguist  and you know and as i look at this book  i mean all the things that i wrote in  2003 there's hardly anything there that  i would have changed i'm s it's still  the same thing uh you have to be  motivated to learn a language uh the  world is full of potential linguists  people who could easily learn to speak  more than one language and who would  derive great enjoyment from it i'm  motivated to i'm an activist i want  there to be more linguists i want i even  want the word linguist which really only  means someone who speaks more than one  language it only has that meaning  apparently in english in all other  languages  the word has been hijacked  by these linguistics people  to mean someone who is a  specialist in the field of linguistics i  would 